    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all 3 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional `postcode` field for owners so it fully satisfies the spec, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` property (`type: string`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf` including `OwnerFields`, the field is both accepted on create and returned on read, and the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` now carry a `postcode` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `postcode` column (`@Column(name = \"postcode\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it automatically both ways (DTO \u2194 entity \u2194 response DTO), so it's stored and returned when given.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `postcode` column. hsqldb is the one the tests actually use (ddl-auto is `none`), the others updated for consistency.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 Made the class and its `derive(city)` method `public` so the controller can reuse the existing city\u2192region table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) instead of duplicating it.\n\n5. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGE` table (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) and a `validatePostcode(...)` step in `addOwner`. When a postcode is present it must be exactly 4 digits and, if the city derives to a known region, within that region's range; otherwise it's rejected with **400** (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException` naming `postcode`), matching how the other field validations report. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode, and an absent postcode is skipped entirely \u2014 so previously-valid minimal owners still pass.\n\nAll tests green (`Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
